      "text": "To solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), we start by expressing \\(g(f(x))\\) in terms of \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(x\\). Given that \\(f(x) = ax + b\\) and \\(g(x) = 2x - 5\\), we substitute \\(f(x)\\) into \\(g(x)\\):\n\n\\[\ng(f(x)) = g(ax + b) = 2(ax + b) - 5 = 2ax + 2b - 5\n\\]\n\nWe know from the problem statement that \\(g(f(x)) = 3x + 4\\) for all \\(x\\). Therefore, we can equate the expressions:\n\n\\[\n2ax + 2b - 5 = 3x + 4\n\\]\n\nFor the above equation to hold for all \\(x\\), the coefficients of \\(x\\) and the constant terms on both sides must be equal. This gives us the following system of equations:\n\n\\[\n2a = 3\n\\]\n\\[\n2b - 5 = 4\n\\]\n\nSolving the first equation for \\(a\\):\n\n\\[\n2a = 3 \\implies a = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSolving the second equation for \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n2b - 5 = 4 \\implies 2b = 9 \\implies b = \\frac{9}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\(a + b\\):\n\n\\[\na + b = \\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{9}{2} = \\frac{3 + 9}{2} = \\frac{12}{2} = 6\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a + b\\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
